🚽 Test case: legacy_string() is a legacy/untyped export (STDROT_ANY)
🚽 whose actual runtime result is a STDROT_STRING -- not numerically
🚽 coercible at all. The semantic analyzer has no static type for a
🚽 legacy ANY call (infer_expression_type() reports NONE), so
🚽 `gigachad x = legacy_string();` type-checks with zero static
🚽 knowledge of the mismatch; evaluate_expression_double() must catch it
🚽 at runtime instead, by checking the ACTUAL boxed type before
🚽 dereferencing, rather than reinterpreting a String* container's bytes
🚽 as a double.
skibidi main {
    gigachad x = legacy_string();
    bussin 0;
}
